{"conversation_id":"f908af72-cc48-4a29-ac0a-56dd5e9e9d5d","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Root Cause\n\nIn [`pkg/cache.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/cache.py#L4-L5), `_key(spec)` converted the dictionary's items to a tuple directly via `tuple(spec.items())`:\n\n```python\ndef _key(spec):\n    return tuple(spec.items())\n```\n\nBecause dictionary iteration preserves insertion order, two dictionaries with identical key-value pairs inserted in different orders (such as `{\"region\": \"eu\", \"tier\": \"gold\"}` and `{\"tier\": \"gold\", \"region\": \"eu\"}`) yielded different tuple keys. Consequently, looking up `spec_b` resulted in a cache miss (`None`) instead of retrieving the cached value.\n\n### Fix\n\nUpdated [`_key(spec)`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/cache.py#L4-L5) in [`pkg/cache.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/cache.py) to sort items before converting them to a tuple:\n\n```python\ndef _key(spec):\n    return tuple(sorted(spec.items()))\n```\n\n### Verification\n\n- Ran `python -m pytest test_cache.py test_smoke.py`: all 4 tests pass.\n- Verified test files remain unmodified.\n","duration_seconds":113.6592039,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":293739,"output_tokens":6809,"thinking_tokens":4079,"cache_read_tokens":485016,"total_tokens":300548}}
